<title>USA: U.S. exchanges to adopt French electronic system.</title>
<headline>U.S. exchanges to adopt French electronic system.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Chicago Mercantile Exchange (CME) and the New York Mercantile Exchange (NYMEX) said they have signed a letter of intent to adopt the NSC electronic trading system developed by SBF-Paris Bourse and Matif SA.</p>
<p>In return, the Paris markets will adopt the Clearing 21 system developed jointly by the CME and NYMEX.</p>
<p>&quot;This agreement between the French and American exchanges aims to respond to the needs and demands of the international financial community for cost efficiencies, harmonization and standardization of the financial markets' systems,&quot; the exchanges said in a statement.</p>
</text>
